From e3aabdb9ca45fe66b68293ee52078cac05c3b0b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:48:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware page: fix the mesh node list and add a push-update
 button

Field report: AiMesh nodes do not appear on the firmware page for some models
while they do for others (the BE98 was named as one that works).

ONE DEFECT IS PROVABLE FROM THE SOURCE, and it is ours. renderNodes() filtered
the controller out of the list with

    if(String(nd.level || '') === '0') continue;   /* level 0 is the CAP */

but ej_get_cfg_clientlist() emits no "level" key at all - the string does not
appear anywhere in web.c's output. The test therefore never matched and THIS
ROUTER was rendered as one of its own mesh nodes. The stock page filters by
ARRAY INDEX instead ("if(idx == "0") continue;//filter CAP"), because entry 0
being the controller is the contract of that hook. Matched to stock.

That defect inflates the list rather than emptying it, so it does not by itself
explain a missing-nodes report. The rest of what is observable without a live
mesh is that the two empty outcomes were indistinguishable: a failed/unparseable
hook response and a genuinely empty client table both produced one generic
message. They are different faults - the second means cfg_server has not synced
or this router is not a controller - so they now say different things. That
turns "some models show nodes, some do not" into something a report can pin
down.

Also adds the push-update button that was asked for. It calls
"/apply.cgi?action_mode=firmware_upgrade", which is exactly what stock's own
AiMesh upgrade button does (cfgsync_firmware_upgrade in
Advanced_FirmwareUpgrade_Content.asp): cfg_server distributes the firmware to
every connected node. Being a cfgsync operation it needs no per-node URL, so
unlike opening a node's own page it does not depend on that node advertising
local_access - which is the mechanism most likely behind the per-model
difference in the first place.

NOT FIXED, and stated rather than guessed: the existing per-node "open" button
builds its URL without stock's aimesh_get_node_capability(...).local_access
check, so for a node that does not advertise local access it can produce the
wrong scheme/port. Confirming that needs a live multi-node mesh, which is also
what any remaining root cause for the missing-nodes report needs.

RFWU_40..44 seeded English into all 25 packs, lockstep at 6524 lines. All page
tokens resolve; reaper_langcheck 0 breakers; both reaper pages parse under node
in all 25 languages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
